//****************************************************************************
// $Module type: Class Package
// $Module name: cFTDockArea
// $Author     : Nils Svedmyr, RDC Tools International, <mailto:support@rdctools.com>
// Web-site    : http://www.rdctools.com
// Created     : 2026-09-21
//
// Description : The root class of a bottom-dock AREA file - CompilerOutputFT.dg, ModAnalyzerFT.dg,
//               ManualChangesFT.dg - each a Container3d that OutputDockFT.dg #Include's INSIDE
//               oOutputDock_dg, so the area object is constructed as a child of the dock.
//
//               At runtime this class adds nothing to Container3d. It exists for the Studio's
//               Windows Designer, which needs two things the fragment shape denies it:
//
//               1. The Designer models a file only when one of its ROOT-level objects carries a
//                  top-level designer class (Studio help, "How the Studio visually models
//                  objects"). Container3d's own tag is cDTContainer3d, a child container, so an
//                  area file opened on its own answered "No Objects to Model".
//               2. The Designer does not expand #Include, so the areas are not seen through the
//                  dock either: OutputDockFT.dg models as the tab strip alone (Nils 2026-09-21).
//
//               The DesignerClass meta-tag below is the whole fix: a comment to the compiler, an
//               instruction to the Designer. cDTPanel is the plain top-level window - no MDI
//               client (cDTView) and no modal semantics (cDTModalPanel) - so an area models as a
//               window holding its grid and buttons, which is what it is inside the dock. If the
//               Designer ever objects to a Container3d wearing a panel's tag, cDTView is the
//               alternative; the tag is the only line to change.
//
//               Each area file Use's this package for itself (a once-only no-op when the dock has
//               Used it first), and OutputDockFT.dg Use's it BEFORE the #Include lines - the one
//               that matters: a Use inside the dock's object body would paste this class
//               definition into the object.
//
// This code is distributed in the hope that it will be useful, but WITHOUT ANY WARRANTY;
// without even the implied warranty of MERCHANTABILITY or FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE.
//****************************************************************************
Use Windows.pkg

{ DesignerClass=cDTPanel }
Class cFTDockArea is a Container3d

    Procedure Construct_Object
        Forward Send Construct_Object
    End_Procedure

End_Class
